1
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,440
‪FEBUREZE, 99% ODOR REMOVAL
‪TASTY RICE CRACKERS

2
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:43,370
‪Deodorizing spray?

3
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,690
‪Um, Yamada…

4
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:47,950
‪Do I…

5
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:52,370
‪Um… Uh… So…

6
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:56,410
‪Sorry. Never mind.

7
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,460
‪With the bag, that comes to 1, 563 yen.

8
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:04,590
‪Okay.

9
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:08,470
‪This isn't really something you ask
‪someone while they're on their shift…

10
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:13,980
‪Here is your change.

11
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:16,480
‪Thank you, and have a nice day.

12
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,480
‪Thanks.

13
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:26,320
‪Toxic workplace.

14
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,700
‪Toxic boss.

15
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,700
‪Deodorizing products.

16
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,990
‪Something he wanted to ask.

17
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:41,000
‪Could it be…

18
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:44,000
‪Sasaki.

19
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:46,260
‪Were you accused
‪of smelling like cigarettes?

20
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:52,220
‪Tayama, are you psychic or something?

21
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:57,190
‪You must think everyone
‪around you is psychic.

22
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,890
‪I saw you buying deodorizing spray
‪while out on the sales floor.

23
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,230
‪Wha… When did you see me?

24
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,530
‪Well, it's not a lie…

25
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,780
‪Yeah. You got it.

26
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:15,660
‪The boss is a militant nonsmoker, 
‪and he yelled at me to "Fix that smell."

27
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:17,330
‪Damn, I'm good.

28
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,170
‪Well, that's a smoker's lot in life.

29
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,600
‪Brush your teeth after you smoke.
‪That should get rid of the smell.

30
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:36,100
‪Then all that's left to do
‪is to just spray down your clothes.

31
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,100
‪But even then…

32
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:43,350
‪some people might still complain, 
‪like they did for me--

33
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,770
‪Tayama, you're amazing!

34
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:49,200
‪That's so cool
‪that you know all this stuff!

35
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,200
‪Not really.

36
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,160
‪Just a few tips I picked up from a senior.

37
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:59,620
‪And now you're the one to teach me.

38
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,840
‪Sasaki. Shake.

39
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,090
‪Huh? Oh, sure.

40
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:13,430
‪Hey, wait. "Shake"?

41
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:15,140
‪Tayama?

42
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,850
‪This is for you.

43
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:21,100
‪It's a deodorizing mist that I use.

44
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:24,730
‪Whoa… It looks expensive. Are you sure?

45
00:04:24,810 --> 00:04:27,730
‪It's used, and I have more at home.
‪Just take it.

46
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,900
‪Thank you.

47
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:32,870
‪I'm going to feel very stylish.

48
00:04:33,450 --> 00:04:36,250
‪It's mild enough
‪that you can use it regularly

49
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,030
‪without bothering your workmates.

50
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,420
‪Wow, so it's scented?

51
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,080
‪What does it smell like?

52
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:46,130
‪Wanna check?

53
00:04:48,130 --> 00:04:51,010
‪I sprayed some around here, so go ahead.

54
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:55,260
‪I'm not going to sniff you!

55
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,520
‪I thought you'd take the bait
‪and go in for a sniff.

56
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:05,030
‪Tayama, do you think
‪I'm a dog or something?

57
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:13,030
‪A Labrador retriever, maybe?

58
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:16,280
‪Huh? A Labra-what?

59
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,570
‪-It's a dog.
‪-You really do think I'm a dog!

60
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:24,040
‪HAPPY CORP.

61
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,040
‪COMPANY MOTTO
‪"NEVER REST…"

62
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:45,400
‪Now, just to spray myself with this…

63
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:51,950
‪Actually, how much should I be putting on?

64
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:55,530
‪I tend to just do a quick spritz
‪with the deodorizing spray.

65
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:58,660
‪You sure do take
‪your public image to heart.

66
00:05:58,740 --> 00:05:59,570
‪Suzuki!

67
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:06,670
‪Telling smokers they stink is just
‪the manager's version of "good morning."

68
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,880
‪You take everything too literally.

69
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:11,880
‪Yes, but!

70
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:16,220
‪Apparently if you brush your teeth after
‪smoking and spritz some deodorizing mist…

71
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:20,390
‪Voilà! Instant odor control.
‪Or so I've been told.

72
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:22,640
‪You've been told? By whom?

73
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:25,470
‪Well, uh…

74
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,820
‪TAYAMA - STORE CLERK
‪WE SMOKE TOGETHER

75
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:28,890
‪Go on. Introduce me.

76
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:36,240
‪That's cold! Why the hell would you--

77
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,950
‪Wow, that does smell good!

78
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:43,540
‪I'll bet the wife will fall head
‪over heels for you smelling this good.

79
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,870
‪You magnificent fool…

80
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,050
‪Keiko is already head over heels for me.

81
00:06:50,670 --> 00:06:54,670
‪But, hey, there's no harm
‪in raising the bar. Am I right?

82
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,550
‪Tell me more.

83
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:03,720
‪It's like I said. You just brush
‪your teeth and spray some mist.

84
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:05,810
‪Just a little spritz, like this…

85
00:07:08,770 --> 00:07:09,770
‪SUPER S
‪OPEN 24 HOURS

86
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:11,310
‪Hello, and welcome!

87
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,940
‪Here is your change.

88
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,810
‪Thank you.

89
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:17,940
‪Oh?

90
00:07:18,030 --> 00:07:20,740
‪Sasaki, something's different today.

91
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:24,160
‪You kind of smell like Tayama.

92
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,080
‪Wait, I…

93
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,840
‪I'm so embarrassed!

94
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,920
‪She gave me a mist spray the other day.

95
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,460
‪But I never found out
‪how much you're supposed to spray.

96
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:41,050
‪Guess I sprayed a little too much.

97
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:50,350
‪Sorry! Thank you very much!

98
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:57,150
‪Yamada, you're good to go now.

99
00:07:58,150 --> 00:08:01,490
‪-Are you okay? Is something wrong?
‪-Oh…

100
00:08:02,450 --> 00:08:05,750
‪I went to tease someone, but…

101
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:09,920
‪But it actually backfired on me.

102
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:01,550
‪It's nice, isn't it?

103
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:05,810
‪RESTROOM
‪ELEVATOR

104
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,820
‪All hail Master Tayama.

105
00:09:25,910 --> 00:09:27,700
‪ETIQUETTE MASTER

106
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:32,250
‪I hope she likes my token of thanks.

107
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:39,460
‪Tayama, good eve…

108
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:47,970
‪Another employee?

109
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:12,330
‪And you are?

110
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,500
‪My name is Sasaki.

111
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,120
‪Well, well. Sasaki, is it?

112
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,630
‪You seem like a suspicious chap.
‪I'm calling the cops.

113
00:10:25,050 --> 00:10:28,640
‪No, please! Wait!
‪I'm an acquaintance of Tayama!

114
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:31,220
‪I was wandering around, 
‪looking for a place to smoke, 

115
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,300
‪when Tayama was kind enough
‪to invite me over.

116
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:37,520
‪And so I've just been going
‪along with her offer ever since.

117
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:42,700
‪Who's "Tayama"?

118
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:46,110
‪And actually, I know this chap…

119
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:50,690
‪This is the guy who's always lining up and
‪smiling like a goose at Yamada's register.

120
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:52,490
‪MY DOG BETH

121
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:55,330
‪I remember, because he looks
‪just like the family dog back home.

122
00:10:55,410 --> 00:10:56,410
‪But who is "Tayama"?

123
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,750
‪Don't you mean Yamada?

124
00:10:58,830 --> 00:11:01,920
‪Why do you bring Yamada into this?

125
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,840
‪I mean Tayama.

126
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:08,170
‪She's a young lady, mature for her age, 
‪and she wears a cool jacket.

127
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:11,680
‪She said she's friends with Yamada.

128
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,970
‪Oh. This chap's getting played.

129
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:25,860
‪So you're here for another smoke
‪with Yama… Yama…

130
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:28,070
‪I mean, "Tayama" tonight?

131
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:31,900
‪Oh, no. I just came to give her something.

132
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:33,080
‪Something?

133
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,450
‪Has she got you as her sugar daddy?

134
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:39,210
‪It's a thank-you gift!

135
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,580
‪A thank-you gift?

136
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:47,340
‪Tayama should be out soon.

137
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,960
‪Want me to go get her?

138
00:11:49,050 --> 00:11:51,300
‪Oh, no. You don't have to do that.

139
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:54,720
‪I was only going to give it to her
‪if she just happened to be around.

140
00:11:55,680 --> 00:12:00,480
‪I'm sorry to trouble you, but could you
‪perhaps give it to her instead?

141
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:03,150
‪She'll know what it's for.

142
00:12:08,070 --> 00:12:10,660
‪Sorry to bother you on your break.

143
00:12:13,910 --> 00:12:16,660
‪He really does look like the family dog.

144
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,330
‪Beth!

145
00:12:20,290 --> 00:12:21,880
‪Goto.

146
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:33,260
‪Where was my invitation
‪for this little smoke break?

147
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:43,140
‪Yamada. I've got a bone to pick with you.

148
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:45,070
‪Huh? What'd I do?

149
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:48,110
‪You've been out here smoking
‪with customers, haven't you?

150
00:12:52,450 --> 00:12:53,530
‪I wasn't smoking.

151
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:55,150
‪You're a liar, Yamada!

152
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,700
‪Don't even try to deny it.

153
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,950
‪I already heard about it
‪from a Mr. Sasaki.

154
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,540
‪Was he here?

155
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,580
‪He just left.

156
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:07,000
‪Unbelievable. I almost
‪reported him for suspicious activity.

157
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:10,750
‪He said to give this to "Tayama."

158
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:17,470
‪Something about it being a thank-you gift.

159
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:19,800
‪That's you, right? "Tayama."

160
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:26,100
‪And talk about lazy.

161
00:13:26,190 --> 00:13:28,150
‪"Tayama" and "Yamada"?

162
00:13:28,230 --> 00:13:30,730
‪I'll bet he's the only chap
‪to fall for that.

163
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:34,690
‪You shouldn't be messing around so much
‪with a nice old chap like him.

164
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:37,700
‪Hey, are you even listening--

165
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:41,000
‪I told him it was nothing.

166
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:48,000
‪Oh, I see what this is.

167
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:52,710
‪GOTO'S STORE MANAGER METER
‪SENSE FOR ROMANCE VS. MORALITY

168
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:56,760
‪This is just the sort of entertainment
‪you want on a boring night shift…

169
00:13:57,390 --> 00:13:58,980
‪I'll let 'em be for a while.

170
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:18,280
‪I left in such a hurry.

171
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,860
‪I hope Tayama didn't get in trouble.

172
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:25,130
‪Don't go bringing in strays!

173
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:27,540
‪I'm sorry for bringing him.

174
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,420
‪I'm confiscating your present!

175
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,290
‪You're too cruel…

176
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:35,090
‪No more smoking for you!

177
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:37,260
‪Have you no mercy?

178
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:45,230
‪I'D LOVE FOR YOU
‪TO SLICE MY WATERMELON EVERY DAY

179
00:14:53,190 --> 00:14:57,280
‪Who'd have thought the melon plot
‪would rear its head up again?

180
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,490
‪I can't wait for the next volume.

181
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:02,700
‪Which one do I read next?

182
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,490
‪LIBRARY
‪THE CATCHER IN THE MELON PATCH

183
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:12,500
‪Oh. It's you, Yamada.

184
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:14,260
‪Hello.

185
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:17,220
‪I thought you were
‪only on the night shift today?

186
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:20,390
‪Chief Maezawa was struggling
‪to put the schedule together, 

187
00:15:20,470 --> 00:15:21,970
‪so here I am anyway.

188
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:25,770
‪And you're logging your hours properly?

189
00:15:25,850 --> 00:15:28,020
‪Yep. All done and dusted.

190
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,780
‪Good girl.

191
00:15:30,850 --> 00:15:32,440
‪Hey, Goto.

192
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:35,770
‪You really have given up
‪on paper cigarettes, haven't you?

193
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:41,660
‪Yeah.

194
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:46,040
‪This is way more socially acceptable.

195
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:49,040
‪And I got sick of spritzing myself down
‪and brushing my teeth after.

196
00:15:51,170 --> 00:15:53,670
‪Says the one who taught me all that.

197
00:15:57,460 --> 00:16:00,460
‪Well? There's no point
‪beating around the bush.

198
00:16:01,090 --> 00:16:03,630
‪If you've got something to say, 
‪just spit it out.

199
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,720
‪YAMA-GULP

200
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:10,190
‪It's just… I never did ask whether
‪it was okay to keep smoking out back.

201
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:12,650
‪Huh? Oh.

202
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:14,820
‪You mean with that old chap?

203
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:19,820
‪You didn't not report him so you could
‪"dispose" of him in your own way, right?

204
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,820
‪You didn't bury him
‪out back somewhere, did you?

205
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,820
‪Where do you want the bullet hole? Well?

206
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:28,080
‪Anywhere but the lungs!

207
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:30,120
‪Why would I do that?

208
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:32,370
‪It may have been in one ear
‪and out the other for you, 

209
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:35,420
‪but all I said was
‪you shouldn't mess with him "so much."

210
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,340
‪"So much." Meaning do it in moderation.

211
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:42,800
‪I'm letting it slide because it's on your
‪own time and it's not holding up the team.

212
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:46,050
‪But if you do go beyond what I consider
‪"in moderation, " I'll put a stop to it.

213
00:16:46,930 --> 00:16:48,520
‪Otherwise, you're fine.

214
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,350
‪End of story.

215
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:53,810
‪Lucky me!

216
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:55,730
‪Hey, Yamada!

217
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:01,110
‪You tell me if anything happens, y'hear?

218
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:06,369
‪Sure, but… What's going to happen?

219
00:17:06,950 --> 00:17:08,619
‪Isn't it obvious?

220
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:12,619
‪You tell me if your heart
‪starts leaping for joy.

221
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,710
‪Okay. See you later.

222
00:17:24,430 --> 00:17:28,140
‪I really ought to give her
‪a proper apology.

223
00:17:29,180 --> 00:17:31,350
‪And all I wanted was to thank her.

224
00:17:31,430 --> 00:17:34,140
‪Who do I think I am, causing her trouble?

225
00:17:34,230 --> 00:17:35,400
‪You're suspicious.

226
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,650
‪Forgive me!

227
00:17:39,270 --> 00:17:40,350
‪Tayama?

228
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:43,150
‪What are you doing, being all sneaky like?

229
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:47,700
‪I ran into another employee
‪here the other day.

230
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:50,620
‪You didn't get in trouble, did you?

231
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,660
‪Oh. You met the store manager.

232
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:54,910
‪Store manager?

233
00:17:55,790 --> 00:17:57,920
‪It wasn't a big deal.

234
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,130
‪And more importantly, come here.

235
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:01,920
‪Hey, wait--

236
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,670
‪You mean the store manager
‪said it was okay to smoke here?

237
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,680
‪She said it was fine in moderation.

238
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,390
‪"In moderation…"

239
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:13,690
‪That doesn't sound
‪like an actual go-ahead…

240
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:33,700
‪Oh, and Sasaki?

241
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:36,700
‪This thing.

242
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:38,460
‪It's cute.

243
00:18:40,290 --> 00:18:44,800
‪You said you didn't want any money, 
‪but I still wanted to thank you.

244
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,920
‪I'm glad you like it.

245
00:18:47,010 --> 00:18:48,220
‪Yeah.

246
00:18:51,510 --> 00:18:55,220
‪Just looking at this thing makes me smile.

247
00:18:55,310 --> 00:18:57,230
‪Oh, really?

248
00:18:57,310 --> 00:19:01,110
‪I imagine you
‪pondering over what to buy for me.

249
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:06,280
‪Why does that make you smile?

250
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:09,860
‪Well, you must have had
‪a tough time finding this, right?

251
00:19:09,950 --> 00:19:13,000
‪It's not easy to find something
‪as cute as this in stores these days.

252
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:24,460
‪So when I think about you asking
‪the store staff where they sell them, 

253
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:28,260
‪and going to the knickknack section
‪that's always full of women, 

254
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:33,970
‪feeling awkward, but pushing through it
‪to find something for me anyway…

255
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,930
‪Tayama, 
‪you really are psychic, aren't you?

256
00:19:48,150 --> 00:19:53,030
‪Well, just picturing it all
‪makes me smile.

257
00:19:54,370 --> 00:19:57,670
‪I think you're just trying
‪to poke fun at an old man.

258
00:19:57,750 --> 00:20:01,550
‪Oh? I wouldn't say that.
‪You make me feel better.

259
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,170
‪I can't tell if she's joking
‪or being serious.

260
00:20:14,510 --> 00:20:15,550
‪Thank you.

261
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:18,310
‪I'll guard this with my life.

262
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,320
‪I guess I don't mind either way.

263
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:25,940
‪Hey, Sasaki.

264
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:29,360
‪Isn't it about time
‪you ash your cigarette?

265
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:32,070
‪You're right.

266
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:34,570
‪You can use this.

267
00:20:35,530 --> 00:20:37,950
‪How good is it
‪that you get to use it right away?

268
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,120
‪Thank yo--

269
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:43,080
‪Isn't that a little close?

270
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:46,090
‪You need to ash it properly, 
‪or else you'll burn yourself.

271
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:47,840
‪Go on then.

272
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:49,830
‪Ash it.

273
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,130
‪No…

274
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:55,060
‪You could just hand it to me.

275
00:20:55,140 --> 00:20:57,350
‪Then go on and take it.

276
00:20:59,430 --> 00:21:01,100
‪What…

277
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:02,470
‪A little more.

278
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,020
‪More!

279
00:21:08,690 --> 00:21:10,360
‪Tayama.

280
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,940
‪Why are you moving it away from me?

281
00:21:13,450 --> 00:21:15,120
‪I am, aren't I?

282
00:21:16,070 --> 00:21:18,490
‪You sure do have long arms, don't you?

283
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:21,210
‪Come on, Tayama.

284
00:21:21,290 --> 00:21:23,630
‪My arm is gonna…

285
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:37,640
‪Pain relief patches?

286
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:39,890
‪Don't tell me…

287
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:44,270
‪Are you okay?

288
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:45,520
‪I'm fine!

289
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:48,770
‪Sorry, I just choked on air
‪for a second there.

290
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:52,360
‪I really am sorry. Please forgive me.

291
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:55,900
‪Yamada, there's no need
‪for such a big apology.

292
00:21:56,490 --> 00:22:00,410
‪I guess older dudes really do spend
‪more time recovering from a pulled muscle.

293
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:04,080
‪Sasaki, please forgive me…

294
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:07,910
‪It's fine. Everything's fine, Yamada!

295
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,250
‪-Please forgive me.
‪-Please, stop!

296
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:14,050
‪-Please stop apologizing.
‪-I am so terribly sorry.

297
00:22:14,130 --> 00:22:15,920
‪I'm telling you. It's fine!

298
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:39,890
‪Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
